<h3>
	Motivational Interviewing (explain)
</h3>
<section class="callout">
	<p>
		Motivational interviewing is best defined by its developers, Miller & Rollnick - ““Motivational 
		Interviewing is a collaborative, goal-oriented style of communication with particular attention to 
		the language of change. It is designed to strengthen personal motivation for and commitment to a 
		specific goal by eliciting and exploring the person's own reasons for change within an atmosphere 
		of acceptance and compassion.” (Miller & Rollnick, 2013).
	</p>

